## Why This Is Asked
This tests end-to-end real-time monocular 3D pose with online calibration under non-ideal lighting and occlusions, plus efficient 3-shot adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 3D pose under occlusion
- Online camera self-calibration
- Differentiable rendering with photometric losses
- Meta-learning for test-time adaptation
- Edge-GPU real-time constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
function forward(frame, state){
  const [detections, poses] = detector(frame);
  const extrinsics = state.update(detections, poses);
  const losses = photometricLoss(frame, detections, poses, extrinsics);
  return {losses, extrinsics};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle severe specular highlights? 
- How would you evaluate calibration drift over longer runs?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a real-time monocular system integrating segmentation, 3D pose estimation with scene priors, grasp-point planning, and physics-based stability reasoning—plus efficient edge adaptation with minimal shots.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation using environmental priors
- Grasp-point prediction in cluttered scenes
- Differentiable physics modules for stability evaluation
- On-device few-shot adaptation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode outline for the model heads
function forward(img, shelfPrior) {
  const features = backbone(img);
  const segmentation = segmentationHead(features);
  const pose = poseHead(features, shelfPrior);
  const grasp = graspHead(features, pose);
  const stability = physicsPrior(grasp, pose);
  return { segmentation, pose, grasp, stability };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests on-device few-shot adaptation, robust 3D pose in a cluttered retail environment, and strict latency constraints, plus ongoing data drift with weekly new items.

## Key Concepts

- On-device few-shot adaptation with prototypes
- 6-DoF pose from monocular RGB
- Temporal tracking with Kalman filter and data association
- Domain randomization for synthetic-real data
- Efficiency-focused backbone and head design

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-architecture sketch
class PoseHead {
  forward(featROI, box) {
    const phi = mlp(featROI, 128)
    const q = normalize(phi.slice(0,4))
    const t = phi.slice(4,7)
    return { q, t }
  }
}
```

